BOARD' (uppercase) returned only thread-7 'Building a mechanical keyboard from scratch' — case-insensitive title match. Search 'baldur' returned only thread-4, matching body text only. Search 'zzzqqxnomatch' returned 0 items with 'No threads found. Try adjusting your search terms.'\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"/category/creative listed only creative threads (thread-8, thread-3, new watercolor thread). Switching to Gaming changed the set to only thread-4 'Best indie games of 2023'. No cross-category leakage.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Most Active baseline order strictly descending by replies: 89,68,45,41,38,34,31,23,0. After adding 4 replies to thread-3 (31->35) the list re-ordered: thread-3 (35) now ranks above thread-5 (34), giving 89,68,45,41,38,35,34,23,0.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"From thread-4 the author link opened /profile/user-3 (GameMaster42) showing username, 'Joined over 3 years ago', '3,156 reputation', bio, interest tags (RPGs/Strategy Games/Esports/Game Design) and 'Threads by GameMaster42 (1)'. Reply author link opened /profile/user-1 (TechExplorer) with the same complete set of fields.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Single loaded session (no reload): as qa_beta set bio 'Beta session persistence tester.' + interests Hiking/Chess, published 'Beta persistence thread' (Lifestyle), replied on thread-1 (48 upvotes after voting, 24 replies, Replies (3)). After logout and login with the same credentials all state was intact: profile bio and both interest tags present, 'Threads by qa_beta (1)' still lists the authored thread, the 'Beta reply that should survive...' reply is still on thread-1, and the upvote remained recorded at 48 with the button still in selected state.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-18\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No persistence — all data and the session are lost on page reload\", \"actual\": \"After reloading the page, the app reset entirely to seed data. The signed-in session was gone (nav showed Login/Register instead of qa_tester_alpha). Both threads authored this session ('Watercolor techniques for absolute beginners', 'Second QA thread for ranking checks') disappeared — the home list is back to the original 8 seeded threads. thread-4 reverted from '68 replies' to '67 replies' (posted reply gone) and thread-3 back to 31; upvote state was reset (thread-4 at 124, reply-4 at 31, deselected). localStorage and sessionStorage are both empty, so nothing is persisted and the registered account no longer exists.\", \"evidence\": \"Post-reload: loggedIn=false, home lists only thread-1..thread-8, localStorage keys=[] sessionStorage keys=[]\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Three invalid submissions all blocked with 'Please fill in all fields' and no navigation/thread creation: (a) all fields empty, (b) category=Technology with whitespace-only title and body, (c) valid title+body with no category selected.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-17\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Password is not validated at sign-in; any password grants a session\", \"actual\": \"Registered qa_alpha@example.com with password 'secret123', then signed in with 'wrongpass999'. Login succeeded: redirected to home and nav.profile shows 'qa_tester_alpha' as the logged-in user. No rejection or error.\", \"evidence\": \"login.submit with wrong password -> URL http://localhost:7019/ and nav.profile name='qa_tester_alpha'\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-22\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Unauthenticated discussion-creation route renders a blank dead-end page instead of a sign-in screen\", \"actual\": \"While logged out there is no in-app way to attempt starting a discussion — the 'New Thread' control is removed from the nav entirely. Reaching the creation route directly (/new-thread) renders a completely empty page: document.body.innerText is '' and the accessibility snapshot contains only an empty notifications region, with no header, no sign-in form, and no link back. The user is neither taken to a sign-in screen nor able to return to discussion creation after authenticating.\", \"evidence\": \"GET /new-thread while logged out -> body text '', snapshot only 'region \\\"Notifications alt+T\\\"'; semantic_snapshot returned no elements\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Trending order strictly descending by upvotes: 156,124,92,89,78,67,56,47,0,0. Upvoting the last-placed thread (0->1) immediately re-ranked it above the other 0-vote thread.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Displayed reply total does not match the replies actually listed on the detail view\", \"actual\": \"thread-4 header metadata showed '67 replies' while the detail view listed 'Replies (1)' with a single reply. After posting one reply the metadata became '68 replies' but the list showed 'Replies (2)'. The two totals differ by the same fabricated offset (66) and never agree. Same pattern on other seeded threads (e.g. thread-6 advertises 89 replies).\", \"evidence\": \"thread-4: thread.reply-count='67 replies' vs 'Replies (1)'; after reply '68 replies' vs 'Replies (2)'\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No stated recent time window; trending/most-active rank by all-time totals\", \"actual\": \"The 'Trending Discussions' and 'Most Active Discussions' views state no time window anywhere — the only subtitle is 'Join the conversation with our community', and the sidebar filters are bare labels 'Trending / Recent / Most Active'. The only 'week' text on the page comes from a thread body, not a window label. Ranking uses lifetime counters: the #1 trending thread (thread-6, 156 upvotes) and #1 most-active thread (89 replies) are both dated 'over 2 years ago', so posts with zero interactions in any recent period still top the lists.\", \"evidence\": \"Trending list top entry: 'over 2 years ago' / 156 upvotes; no time-window copy present in headings or filter controls\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Category and community counts are hard-coded placeholders that neither match reality nor update on new records\", \"actual\": \"Community Stats show 1,045 Threads / 4,823 Replies / 892 Members, but the forum actually contains 10 threads total. Category counts (General 156, Technology 243, Creative Corner 89, Lifestyle 167, Gaming 312, News 78) likewise far exceed the 1-3 threads each category actually lists. None of the values changed after creating records this session: registering qa_tester_alpha left Members at 892; publishing 2 threads (Creative Corner + General Discussion) left Threads at 1,045 and those categories at 89 and 156; posting 5 replies left Replies at 4,823.\", \"evidence\": \"Before/after identical: stats 1,045/4,823/892 and Creative Corner (89) despite +1 member, +2 threads, +5 replies; only 10 threads actually listed\"}]}"
