    "content": "All 18 checklist items have been executed and recorded — coverage is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n**12 PASS / 6 FAIL**\n\nThe core forum flows work well: registration with duplicate rejection, profile bio/interests editing, thread publishing with category assignment, live replies, single-vote toggling on threads and replies, case-insensitive keyword search across title and body, category filtering, author profile pages, and both Trending (by upvotes) and Most Active (by replies) sorting — including correct live re-ranking when votes or replies change.\n\n**Failures found:**\n\n| ID | Issue |\n|---|---|\n| **CS-17** | *Critical security bug* — password is never validated. Signing in with `wrongpass999` on an account registered with `secret123` granted a full session. |\n| **FT-18** | No persistence at all. A page reload resets the app to seed data: session lost, registered account gone, authored threads/replies/votes wiped. `localStorage` and `sessionStorage` are both empty. |\n| **CS-22** | `/new-thread` while logged out renders a completely blank page — no sign-in screen, no header, no way back. The New Thread control is also hidden from the nav, so there's no in-app path at all. |\n| **CT-19** | Reply totals are fabricated. thread-4 advertised \"67 replies\" while listing \"Replies (1)\"; after posting, \"68 replies\" vs \"Replies (2)\" — a constant offset that never reconciles. |\n| **CT-20** | Trending/Most Active state no recent time window and rank by lifetime counters — the #1 entries in both lists are dated \"over 2 years ago\". |\n| **CT-21** | Category and community counts are hard-coded placeholders (1,045 threads / 4,823 replies / 892 members vs 10 actual threads) and never move when records are created. |\n\nThe most consequential findings are CS-17 and FT-18: together they mean the authentication is decorative and no user data outlives a refresh. CT-19/CT-20/CT-21 share a root cause — inflated seed numbers displayed alongside real, live-computed data, so the two disagree wherever they meet."
  }
